WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.033
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:02.934
This is your first time
on our show.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.367
-I know, finally.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.200
-You do a very funny thing.
I was going to say you did.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.701
You do a very funny thing.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:13.934
You keep buying swag of your
husband when he was Pacey.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:17.000
[ Laughter ]
You buy shirts and wear them
around the house.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.767
And I love that you do it,

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:22.067
but you also wear
his jersey, too,

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.067
from "Mighty Ducks."

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:26.400
[ Laughter ]
Now, does he laugh at it

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.801
or does he like,
"What are you doing?"

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.767
-Well, the funny thing is
that first picture

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.868
that you just showed,
that was the first time

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.167
that he ever saw
what I had done.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.567
So I bought this shirt.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.467
I just love going on Amazon

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.934
and finding things that might
possibly embarrass him,

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:43.901
but also that he secretly loves.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.467
And that was the first time.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.767
So like if you see his face,

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.968
like look at his little face,
he's so embarrassed,

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.901
but he's also loving it so much.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.167
-He does.
He is doing both.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.467
He's embarrassed,
but also like, "This is cool."

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.400
-Yeah, I just come downstairs
with it on

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.033
and then he's like, "Are you --
Is that...?"

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.734
And I'm like, "Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.100
[ Laughter ]
Yeah."
-I also heard that you

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.934
take his swag.

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:06.567
When he was on our show,
we gave a mug and a T-shirt.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.167
-The whole thing is I always
steal my husband's swag,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.701
but the thing is, Jimmy, is now

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.901
I have all that stuff
that you gave him.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.968
-You need more.
-So, now that I'm here,

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.200
I just need you to really bring

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.200
the level up for me.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.033
[ Applause ]
Do you know what I mean?

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.734
I mean, Oprah gives out cars,

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.334
so is there a --
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:27.868
What's under my chair?
-Well, I don't know. Uh --

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.501
-Jimmy, Jimmy, this is --
-This is a mask.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.567
[ Laughter ]
-No, Jimmy.
-Unused. [ Awkward laugh ]

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.300
-Jimmy, that's not good enough.
Come on.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.601
-How about this?
How about --

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:35.834
-No, I have that bag.
-"Tonight Show" tote bag.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.701
[ Audience oohs ]
-I have that.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:38.968
-You have that?
-You gave that to Josh,

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:39.734
okay? Come on.
-Oh.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:40.667
Oh, I have something

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.033
that I did not give to Josh.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.868
[ Audience ohs ]

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.534
How about a Fallon sweatshirt?

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:49.334
You can rock this --
-Getting warmer, getting warmer,

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:50.567
[ Laughter ]
but I feel like it needs --

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.267
I'm talking
about sparkly, shiny.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.701
Look, Oprah gives out

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.234
really good gifts.
-Yeah, but Oprah's not

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.634
on TV that much anymore.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.634
[ Laughter ]
She does specials.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.567
-Jimmy, Jimmy --
Oh!

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:02.200
That's actually terrifying.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.701
[ Laughter ]
But my daughter might enjoy it.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.033
That's something.
-Okay. Mm.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:07.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.300
I accept.
Thank you so much!

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.667
-Act, act like you
love it, please.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.167
-Thank you
[ Whispering ] so much.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.567
-Congrats on "Anne Boleyn."

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:17.934
-[ Clap ] Thank you.
-You're getting great reviews.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:20.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
I mean, this is a big deal.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.167
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.033
-It's on AMC+.

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.868
Is this intimidating,
to take on a real person?

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:32.434
-I was so like ready to tell
a story about mothering

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.467
-Really?
-and so I got really excited

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:36.934
about kind of this idea
of this woman who really,

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:37.934
I mean, it's a mother's story.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.434
She was trying to [bleep]

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:42.434
survive in her time
with the best

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.200
abilities that she could,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.133
that women were allowed to
and, you know,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.234
make women have a seat
at the table.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:52.601
And, really, I mean,
she was a [bleep] disrupter.

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.100
[ Laughter ]
That's what's so amazing
about her

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.634
and I was just like,
"Yes! I get it.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:57.567
I'm an outsider.
I'm a disrupter.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.067
Like yeah!"
-You can't say the f-word

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:00.167
on our show.
-Oh!

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.634
Dude, they're on television.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.534
-I'm sorry.
That was not zen of me.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.234
-But you know what?
It was badass

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.267
and I kind of love that --
-I'm a mother.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.567
I don't use those words.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.400
I'm a mother.
-That's exactly right, yes.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.634
[ Laughter ]
I think you're allowed to do

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.534
whatever you want on my show.
That's the deal.

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.734
I just love having you on here.
That's all I want to say.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you for having me.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.334
-Here's Jodie Turner-Smith
in "Anne Boleyn."

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.667
Take a look at this.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:26.634
-[ Grunts ]

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:27.534
-Is everything alright?

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.601
-Perfectly fine.

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:30.601
Stop fussing.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.601
-Shall I come
to your chambers later?

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:41.400
-And what would be the point?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.968
Until our boy is born,
you have but one job.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.868
Concentrate on that,
if you're so concerned

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.234
with being a good wife.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.601
[ Grunts ]

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.501
[ Grunting ]

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Jodie Turner-Smith, everybody.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.834
The series premiere
of "Anne Boleyn"

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:08.367
is streaming now on AMC+.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.634
New episodes come out
every Thursday.

